ome dramatic  reductions in particularly  hospitalizations and deaths because of  the vaccine taking hold  president biden has said that by the end  of may  every american who wants a vaccine can  get one and i think that is realistic  even with the johnson and johnson pause  i saw some overnight concern in michigan  and other parts of the upper midwest  of the variant there even despite quite  a high degree of vaccination taking  place  something of a sort of a third wave it  was suggested we're not out of the woods  yet if that's happening  no we're not and that that's the fire i  was talking about  um and there are other places in the  united states i mean  really what we've learned from covid um  you know so very clearly  is is that you know it's not so much as  a wave but as a series of forest fires  and so when when one when one  pops out um in one part of the united  states  or the world um and others are feeling  you know quite good about themselves and  complacent  it always moves and you know i do expect  that to happen  you know in the next month um that the  united states as i say is going to be in  a perilous position in that month and we  really do need to be very careful in  terms of  masking and distancing before the  vaccines  really really take hold um but  eventually they will you know and i  i've actually seen this movie before um  with  other major um uh health  health threats things like smallpox  polio even  measles and other childhood vaccinations  when you have  an extraordinarily good set of vaccines  combined with high population coverage  you really can make dramatic differences  and i think  we will over the medium to longer term  what role then do you think vaccine  passports would have in britain  other parts of europe there's quite a  matter of controversy  i'd like to divide it into the official  government vaccine passports is one  possibility which  you may need to cross borders or to get  into the country or  into another country 